Note: CoinDCX’s real-time feeds are provided publicly for REST (order books, trades, candles). Their help/intro references Socket.IO for streaming; you’ll already have the WS endpoint internally. This spec focuses on the shapes and REST fallbacks and assumes your WS messages use the same fields as shown below.

2) Authentication (REST, private)

All private endpoints require:

Header: X-AUTH-APIKEY: <api_key>

Header: X-AUTH-SIGNATURE: <hmac_sha256>

Body: JSON with a timestamp plus endpoint-specific params

Signature is HMAC-SHA256 over the raw JSON body using your secret. 
CoinDCX Docs

Python example (pattern used across endpoints):

body = {"timestamp": int(time.time()*1000), ...}
json_body = json.dumps(body, separators=(',', ':'))
signature = hmac.new(secret_bytes, json_body.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()
headers = {
  "Content-Type": "application/json",
  "X-AUTH-APIKEY": key,
  "X-AUTH-SIGNATURE": signature
}


CoinDCX examples show both “seconds” and code that multiplies by 1000; their examples compute milliseconds. We follow ms consistently. 
CoinDCX

3) Public Market Data (Spot)
3.1 Active markets

GET /exchange/v1/markets (base: api.coindcx.com)
Returns list of active market symbols (e.g., BTCUSDT, BTCINR). Use for symbol hygiene and cross-mapping between USDT↔INR universes. 
CoinDCX

3.2 Market metadata / trading rules

GET /exchange/v1/market_details (base: api.coindcx.com)
Returns per-market trading rules: precisions, min/max quantity/price/notional, allowed order types, pair string (B-<BASE>_<QUOTE>), etc. Use to validate orders & rounding. Key fields:
coindcx_name, symbol, base_currency_precision, target_currency_precision, min_quantity, min_price, min_notional, order_types, pair (e.g., B-BTC_USDT). 
CoinDCX

3.3 Order book (spot)

GET /market_data/orderbook?pair=<PAIR> (base: public.coindcx.com)
pair is the ecode-prefixed name from Market Details, e.g., B-BTC_USDT.
Response: two maps { price: quantity } for bids, asks. Use for bootstrapping your local L2 before switching to sockets. 
CoinDCX

3.4 Recent trades (spot)

GET /market_data/trade_history?pair=<PAIR>&limit=<N> (base: public.coindcx.com)
Items: p (price), q (qty), s (symbol), T (ts ms), m (is maker). Use as a sanity feed & for last price reference. 
CoinDCX Docs

3.5 Candles (spot/futures shared endpoint)

GET /market_data/candles?pair=<PAIR>&interval=<1m|5m|60m|1D>&startTime=&endTime=&limit=
Returns array of bars: open, high, low, volume, close, time. 
CoinDCX Docs

4) Public Market Data (Futures, for parity & structure)

Some futures endpoints are helpful for understanding event schema (same field names are used in socket messages you shared: ts, vs, E, asks, bids, pr, s).

GET /market_data/v3/orderbook/{instrument}-futures/<depth> on public.coindcx.com
Depth: 10|20|50. Response example shows:
ts (timestamp), vs (version), asks/bids as {price: qty} maps. 
CoinDCX

