7) Triangular arbitrage mapping (USDT↔INR)

Use these three legs (example for COIN):

Straight:
INR → USDT (market: USDTINR) → USDT → COIN (market: COINUSDT) → COIN → INR (market: COININR)

Reverse:
INR → COIN (market: COININR) → COIN → USDT (market: COINUSDT) → USDT → INR (market: USDTINR)

Symbols to use come from /exchange/v1/markets; trading rules/precisions from /exchange/v1/market_details. 
CoinDCX
+1

Order types & TIF:

For tight latency and guaranteed execution within spread, prefer IOC (if supported on spot) to avoid resting exposure; CoinDCX help explains IOC semantics. Otherwise use market/limit with conservative slippage caps. 
