9) Socket message schema (Order Book)

Use a single parser for both spot & futures deltas. Fields observed in CoinDCX docs and your sample:

type BookDeltaMsg = {
  ts: number;                   // event time (ms)
  vs: number;                   // version/sequence
  asks: Record<string,string>;  // price -> qty (0 to delete)
  bids: Record<string,string>;
  E?: number;                   // event ts (book-specific)
  pr?: "spot"|"futures";
  s: string;                    // symbol, e.g. "BTCUSDT"
}


Apply price levels in ascending order for asks, descending for bids.

Delete levels where qty is "0" (string zero).

If vs is not prev_vs + 1, consider the feed stale → re-snapshot via REST /market_data/orderbook for that pair and resume. 
CoinDCX
+1

